Title: "Labels"
Id: "62a24a65-05c9-4e09-9722-1eb355fe2ce5"

Text: "Labels identify items inside brackets or nested groups.

```mlg-fragment
[\theorem.ordinal.trichotomy]
Theorem:
then: ...
```

Label headers are parsed from dotted parts. Dots are commonly rendered as spaces in fallback display names, with words capitalized for theorem-like and axiom-like cards.

Label headers differ from expression labels. Expression labels use the `[:label:]` syntax and follow a grouped expression, statement, or specification, while structural label headers appear in square brackets before a group.

```mlg-fragment
(x + y)[:sum:]
(.x is \real.)[:typed:]
```

A `[:label:]` may sit on any nested formulation, and a top-level `Justification:` section discharges it: an entry whose `[label]` heading matches establishes the labeled formulation from its `asserting:` items. Unlike label headers, expression labels are lexer tokens and do not support stropped symbolic parts."
Id: "d36979a8-c1ec-4f3b-8e8c-3dafd5ee366b"
